{
 "subtitle": "7 finished runs, 1.1M env steps each, size50m, one training seed per run. Scored with tools/death_eval.py on the same fixed evaluation worlds. 2026-09-28.",
 "summary": "Every number is the mean episode-final achievement count over the evaluation episodes, and each unlock rate is the share of episodes in which that achievement fired. Every run was scored on the same fixed evaluation worlds. Re-scoring the old 5.80 record and the 2.30 run with today's code reproduced both exactly (same totals, per-achievement rates, death counts and lifespans), so the differences below come from the trained policies, not from how they were measured.\nTwo things look wrong. First, the newest run has the highest total (5.93) but never makes a pickaxe: 0 of 30 episodes, against 9 of 30 for the old record, so it never reaches stone. It makes a wood sword in 60% of episodes instead. The total went up while the tech tree got shallower.\nSecond, every map run unlocks WAKE_UP (sleep, then wake) in 83-98% of episodes; vanilla never does. WAKE_UP is the map runs' whole lead over vanilla: without it the fixed map model scores 4.20 against vanilla's 4.44. Only the potential shaping adds tech-tree progress on top.\nSurvival never moved: every run lives 262-294 steps, inside the random-policy band (261-284), and thirst is the main killer. The non-cheating run (honest_map) is still training after an out-of-memory restart and will be added.",
 "table_note": "eps = evaluation episodes. ach. = mean episode-final achievements; w/o wake = the same minus WAKE_UP. life = mean lifespan in steps. Rates are % of episodes. 'bug' = imag_shift True, which corrupted the policy gradient (fixed 2026-09-20). map_survive was re-evaluated on 2026-09-28 and reproduced its original 2.30. One training seed per run, so the run-to-run spread is unknown. 'Map + potential (fixed)' is the old 5.80 record; 'Control' adds the recipe and death fixes with the privileged map.",
